{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Load the supplied HR LDIF into LDAP on node1 and retain the supplied records under /srv/legacy2/ldap-attribute-privacy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final directory contains the supplied Morgan Lake record with the expected mail and employee number. The retained hr.ldif has the same SHA-256 hash as the preparation baseline and remains present after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-9c47630024884e15","cmd-cc3efe8880ac4f9b","cmd-8b814b60fabc4017","cmd-2e8cc0bd462e41d8"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow the directory-reader identity to search employee names and mail addresses remotely from node2, while preventing it from reading or changing employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Remote node2 searches authenticated as directory-reader returned Morgan Lake and morgan@hr.test without employeeNumber. A reader modification attempt was rejected with LDAP error 50 and left HR-4815 unchanged; the behavior persisted after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c153da132c6543ae","cmd-236a9948b2624e9c","cmd-5e72397a2e614174","cmd-ac87d2d31a28439c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Ensure only the HR administrator may read or change employeeNumber.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"The HR administrator directly demonstrated both read and change access, including restoration of HR-4815, and the reader was denied. However, the separate config-admin identity also directly read employeeNumber, contradicting the strict 'only HR administrator' outcome.","evidence_ids":["cmd-236a9948b2624e9c","cmd-ac87d2d31a28439c","cmd-7c726e49c4684406","cmd-2e8cc0bd462e41d8"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Prevent anonymous users from seeing employee records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous searches from node2 returned zero employee DNs before and after the node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-003b0161cc054220","cmd-c153da132c6543ae","cmd-5e72397a2e614174","cmd-ac87d2d31a28439c"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Provision dedicated demonstration credentials for the reader and HR administrator.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Dedicated reader and administrator LDAP identities were loaded, and separate mode-0600 credential files were present on node1 and node2. Node2's files remained usable after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cc3efe8880ac4f9b","cmd-40a913876be84951","cmd-062d0d69e4ee4495","cmd-ac87d2d31a28439c"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Alpine Linux v3.23 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts. Alpine-packaged OpenLDAP 2.6.13 was installed and functioned after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-db9485793ad345b9","cmd-623a1ef6d33e45aa","cmd-439dfcca3c2e4c86","cmd-5f2676b416e8411d","cmd-8b814b60fabc4017","cmd-ac87d2d31a28439c","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.62,"summary":"Two unnecessary implementation experiments occurred on node1: cmd-80a8a9f8171844a8 created an unrelated synthetic Legacy2 directory/configuration, and cmd-acfb2188fe4e41d2 loaded and briefly served those synthetic Alice/Ben records. The wrong directory, database, and configuration were subsequently replaced and the synthetic supplied-records.ldif removed by cmd-cc3efe8880ac4f9b, so this was reverted apart from credential material later reused by the final solution. The mandatory restart commands left /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log on both nodes (cmd-2d9a16f5cefa45f8 and cmd-0b03930abd044429), confirmed as executor-created residue by the final snapshots. Additionally, slapd remains exposed on all IPv4/IPv6 interfaces using unencrypted ldap:// simple binds, which is an avoidable credential-security weakness even though ACL behavior is correct. Package health shows no executor-caused deterioration.","evidence_ids":["cmd-80a8a9f8171844a8","cmd-acfb2188fe4e41d2","cmd-cc3efe8880ac4f9b","cmd-2d9a16f5cefa45f8","cmd-0b03930abd044429","cmd-24b79986af504a4c","cmd-c153da132c6543ae","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The LDAP directory, remote reader behavior, anonymous restriction, retained source data, demonstration credentials, platform compatibility, and restart persistence were directly demonstrated. The material defect is that employeeNumber access is not exclusive to the HR administrator: the separate config-admin identity can also read it. The provider-wide restart protocol was otherwise complete for both nodes, with matching pre/post boot identities and recovered service, data, credentials, and access behavior.","limitations":["The final evidence verifies the retained supplied hr.ldif directly on node1 but does not re-inventory the prepared copy on node2; the contract's retention location is therefore treated as the node1 directory associated with the LDAP load.","Access behavior was tested for anonymous, directory-reader, HR administrator, and config-admin identities, but not exhaustively for every possible authenticated DN.","OpenRC lacks the systemd failed-unit observation used by the lifecycle collector, so final failed-service coverage is limited to directly checked relevant services."]}
